# Keep LF line endings in the working tree as well as in the repository.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows checks these files out as CRLF and converts
# them back to LF on commit — so every time a tarball rewrites them with LF it
# has to convert every file again, and warns about every file it will convert,
# whether or not that file changed. Reproduced with core.autocrlf=true: two
# files rewritten, one actually different, two warnings.
#
# Nothing here is hand-edited on Windows, so LF everywhere costs nothing and
# the working tree matches what the build produces byte for byte.
* text=auto eol=lf
